## Testing and Verification

When making changes to the codebase, verify them using `npm run lint`

## Code Style

- Never delete pre-existing comments when editing a file
- Do not generate comments
- Never use "any" keyword in TypeScript
- All names of TypeScript interfaces must start with the capital letter I (e.g., IProps, IState)
- Variable names should be complete words, not abbreviations (e.g., "for (const result of results)")
- Files should always end in a newline character
